The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 11 KB). It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit step did nothing, as its || true expects, and the file is on disk for the planner. The build was already green from the harness. My checks: yoyo -p replied pong with exit 0, --version and doctor work, and I ran a probe loop over the shell subcommands.

What I found:
• New issue #1086: 13 shell subcommands print chat-window (REPL) slash syntax in their usage and error text. For example, yoyo find says usage: /find <pattern>, and yoyo run offers !<command>, which doesn't exist in a shell. It's the same class as #1075 and #1083, just 13 times bigger. The issue includes the probe loop, so the count can be driven to 0, plus a two-line comparison: git and cargo both name the binary and the verb in their usage lines.
• #1071 is now waiting on me. @yuanhao did the workflow half this morning (68e9b580) and named my half: add "synthesize" to PHASE_SPEND_PHASES. The blocker is that the first synthesize spend row holds 4 test-model records that came from test runs writing into the real .yoyo/audit.jsonl while YOYO_AUDIT=1 was set. I traced it partway but haven't confirmed the writer. The only place audit logging gets switched on is main.rs:1026, so it must be a spawned binary that inherits the env var. Only 2 test files remove YOYO_AUDIT from the environment before spawning.
• The new yoagent version adds something yoyo doesn't use. yoagent 0.25.15 (merged this morning) can detect a stdio MCP server that has exited (McpClient::exited()) and withdraw its tools (McpToolSource). yoyo connects through with_mcp_server_stdio, which drops the client handle, so a server that dies mid-session keeps its tools on offer and the model keeps calling it. Claude Code tells the model when a server disconnects and has /mcp → Reconnect. I saved this comparison to yopedia; one phrase was lost from the note because of a shell quoting slip.
• Small debts, checked against the current code: the test in tests/hook_feedback_request.rs:300-321 still has the false "own block" name owed on #1054. #1084 has two cost rows that read low against the documented error-direction policy, and format/cost.rs has only 3 lines left under its size cap, so that fix belongs in a sibling module.

The last 5 runs: 4 succeeded and the current one is in progress. The last 10 sessions each finished both tasks, with no reverts and no provider errors. The CI failures in the window are 7 days old and already fixed.

My suggested order for the planner: #1071 (stop the test-model writer, then add the phase), then #1086, then MCP mid-session death, then the small debts.
